//
// Inter-service gRPC contract for the Observability supporting domain
// (chora_observability database, Team 3 / Platform). Wave-1 ADR-140
// remediation per docs/m13/grpc-mass-remediation-2026-05-16.md §4 (owner
// O-FULL): adds the gRPC surface so chora-gateway BFF + chora-governance
// can dial inter-service over mTLS + service mesh instead of plain
// HTTP :8080 (the prior systemic ADR-140 violation).
//
// Aggregates exposed:
//   - TokenUsageLedger     — append-only billing-grade LLM usage ledger;
//                            atomic outbox via ledger.LedgerHook when wired.
//                            Primary write caller: Model Broker Gateway
//                            / ADR-146 successor. Primary read caller:
//                            chora-gateway BFF for the O+ cost dashboard.
//   - AgentDecisionLog     — append-only audit log of agentic decisions
//                            (route / escalate / refuse / respond). Primary
//                            write caller: Governance Gatekeeper agent.
//                            Primary read callers: chora-gateway BFF
//                            (`GET /events` audit-events endpoint) +
//                            chora-governance (IMDA D1/D2 evidence query).
//   - TraceCorrelation     — correlation_id → (trace_id, parent_span_id,
//                            child_spans[]) binding so downstream consumers
//                            can walk a cross-service Pub/Sub fanout back
//                            to the originating request.
//
// REST surfaces in services/chora-observability/internal/adapter/http/
// remain LIVE in parallel through Wave-3 soak per the same doc §7 risk +
// rollback ruling. gRPC is for internal service-to-service sync only;
// learner/admin-facing UI continues to use the REST surface through
// chora-gateway (which itself switches BFF → gRPC in Wave 2).
//
// Cross-DB queries FORBIDDEN — every cross-domain dependency is wired
// via Pub/Sub events (e.g. token_usage.recorded.v1 outbox row).
//
// Deployed in chora-local team-platform pool. mTLS via the service mesh;
// SPIFFE identity in mesh; W3C trace context in gRPC metadata.
// =============================================================================

